# Paths that must NEVER be uploaded to lulhaven.com. Patterns are rsync patterns.
#
# HOW THIS FILE IS USED (root cause found 2026-07-31, challenge.db #102):
# `.assetsignore` is a Cloudflare WORKERS Static Assets feature. `wrangler pages
# deploy` does NOT read it — Pages only auto-excludes node_modules, .DS_Store
# and .git, and offers no user-supplied ignore file at all. So for months every
# pattern here was decorative and every listed path was publicly fetchable.
# deploy-lulhaven.sh now honours this file ITSELF: it stages a filtered copy of
# the site and uploads that. Do not assume Cloudflare reads this file.
#
# The underlying problem it guards: the site directory is a WORKING directory
# (source trees, schemas, editor backups and tool config all live in it) and the
# publish step uploads whatever happens to be sitting there.

# --- editor / reversibility backups (Dave's .BAK convention keeps these in place)
*.BAK*
**/*.BAK*

# --- source trees that are not website content
adq
adq/**
migrations
migrations/**

# --- database schemas: never content, and they map our storage for anyone
*.sql
**/*.sql

# --- tool + repo configuration. wrangler.toml names the D1/R2 bindings and the
#     BUILD_MAINT_PASSWORD secret; publishing it hands out the attack map.
wrangler.toml
# --- local-dev secret env files (Cloudflare Workers). .dev.vars held a real
#     CONTEST_ACCOUNT_KEY and was publicly served on lulhaven.com until it was
#     caught by the Hearst live-exclusion check 2026-08-19 — never ship these.
.dev.vars
**/.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
.env
.env.*
*.env
.assetsignore
.gitignore
.git
.wrangler
node_modules
.DS_Store

# --- agent instructions / notes
CLAUDE.md
.claude
